<newsitem itemid="23004" id="root" date="1996-08-29" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Slough Estates H1 pretax profit 37 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Slough Estates H1 pretax profit 37 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		5.7		    vs 4.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.25		   vs 3.1</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    37.4		   vs 32.8</p>
<p> Turnover		   109.0		  vs 88.6</p>
<p> Operating profit	 67.2		   vs 58.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Property company Slough Estates Plc said the property sector should continue to improve and the group was &quot;in a strong position to reap the benefits&quot;.  </p>
<p> Interest paid	    31.1		   vs 28.9</p>
<p> Tax paid		   9.4		    vs 7.5</p>
<p> Net taxed		  28.0		   vs 25.3</p>
<p> Attributable	     22.1		   vs 19.3</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 11, 1996</p>
<p> Div  registration date September 17, 1996</p>
<p> Ex-div date		September 9, 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Property investment income for the period was 67.5 million stg, 3.6 million stg higher than for the same period the previous year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
